cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, as well as the papers describing the statistical models (see 'references')."
type: software
title: "vgi4bio: Capitalizing on Opportunistic Data for Monitoring Relative Abundances of Species"
abstract: >-
  R package providing functions, data sets and examples to estimate relative
  species abundances and their habitat preferences by combining opportunistic
  data (e.g. citizen science) with standardized monitoring data. It implements
  the generalized linear model of Giraud et al. (2016) and the Bayesian model
  of Coron et al. (2018), the latter with JAGS or a Hamiltonian Monte Carlo
  (NUTS) sampler from nimble. Developed within the ANR project VGI4BIO.
